part.text:
Created `app/page.tsx` using `connection()` from `next/server` — Next.js's recommended approach for opting out of static prerendering without cookies/headers.

```tsx
import { connection } from 'next/server'

export default async function Home() {
  await connection()
  const timestamp = new Date().toISOString()

  return (
    <main>
      <h1>Server Timestamp</h1>
      <p>Current server time: {timestamp}</p>
    </main>
  )
}
```

Build confirms the route is dynamic (`ƒ`) and server-rendered on demand, so the timestamp will be fresh on every request.
